From d10b699b6fd5f7acc0d29b0660dc9b7be30ead13 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 12:06:16 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] Worker pickup skips a card the local dispatcher
 would hold on its quota wall

worker-3 2026-11-12 11:30-11:56Z: four foreign cards walled until 11-17/18
(subscription_quota_reset) were first in candidate order and filled every
pickup batch. Each tick copied them, local dispatch held them, the next tick
evicted and copied them again (126 pickups in 26 min), and two priority-0
cards pinned to the machine waited budget_exhausted (t_01a1cf9f2b838cbb).

_evaluate now asks, before spending budget on a candidate, whether the local
dispatcher would hold it on its quota episode: the same read-only
kanban_quota_episode.decision that check_respawn_guard returns for a card with
an episode, judged on the card's runs/events in the replica (a copy carries
exactly those) and this machine's provider walls. Such a card is not copied
and takes no budget; when it is pinned here, its pickup skip records
`hold: subscription_quota_reset until <deadline>` instead of budget_exhausted.
An episode with a free alternate route, or a past deadline, is copied as
before, and any failure of the check copies as before (the local guard still
decides after the copy). active_pr holds are left to eba518b16a (a held copy
is kept, not re-imported): predicting them needs PR state from gh per
candidate per tick.

Candidate order is unchanged (DISPATCH_ORDER, parity with the hub): only
cards that would never spawn here leave the batch, so no reordering of
machine-pinned cards is needed.

Proof:
- tests/hermes_cli/test_kanban_pickup_quota_held.py: 3 walled cards ahead of
  a priority-0 pinned card, budget 2. Base: the first tick imports two walled
  cards instead (RED). After: the first tick imports and starts the pinned
  card, 3 more ticks import nothing, the pinned walled card records `hold`;
  parity assertion that check_respawn_guard on a copy returns
  subscription_quota_reset. A passed deadline and a failing check copy.
- 76 test files importing kanban_worker_node / kanban_quota_episode: 1724 passed.
